{"id":3935,"date":"2021-10-25T14:00:59","date_gmt":"2021-10-25T21:00:59","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=3935"},"modified":"2025-10-23T13:16:18","modified_gmt":"2025-10-23T20:16:18","slug":"1-2-flight-events-junior-cde-blockly","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/1-2-flight-events-junior-cde-blockly\/","title":{"rendered":"1.2: Flight Commands"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213371156e\" name=\"6a2213371156e\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>We've Moved!<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1761250576975{padding-top: 20px !important;padding-right: 20px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;padding-left: 20px !important;background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-11766\" src=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/icon_warning-150x150-2-84x85.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"81\" height=\"82\" \/><\/p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"><strong>We\u2019ve moved to our new lesson portal: <a href=\"http:\/\/learn.robolink.com\">Robolink Learn<\/a>! Lessons here will remain available until the end of June 2026. This version of Basecamp will no longer be updated and uses outdated references to Blockly for Robolink. You can access the previous version of <a href=\"https:\/\/codrone.robolink.com\/edu\/blockly-archive\/\">Blockly here<\/a>.<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221337116b3\" name=\"6a221337116b3\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Getting Started<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Make sure that your drone is connected with <a href=\"https:\/\/codrone.robolink.com\/edu\/blockly-archive\/\">Blockly<\/a> before starting the lesson! If you are unsure of how to connect, go back to <a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/0-1-connecting-and-coding-with-cde-blockly\/\">the first lesson<\/a> to review![\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22133711724\" name=\"6a22133711724\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Flight Commands<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div>Out of all the menus in Blockly, the one you will be using the most is &#8220;Flight Commands&#8221;. This is where you will find blocks to have your CoDrone EDU fly in different directions and, probably most important, take off and land! To find the <strong>take off<\/strong> and <strong>land<\/strong> blocks, click on the dark blue flight commands menu.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7553&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22133711794\" name=\"6a22133711794\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Take Off<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div>Any code that has your CoDrone EDU in the air will start with the <strong>take off<\/strong> block. This will make your drone launch from the ground. Don\u2019t worry about your drone flying straight into the ceiling! CoDrone EDU uses the height sensor to fly about a meter off of the ground. Then, it will hover automatically and wait for the next command.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7915&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Drag the <strong>take off<\/strong> block from the flight commands menu to your workspace.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7917&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221337117eb\" name=\"6a221337117eb\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Land<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The <strong>land<\/strong> block brings your CoDrone EDU to the ground gently. When you\u2019re finished with everything else in your code, attach the <strong>land<\/strong> block to the bottom of your program.\u00a0<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7945&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213371183f\" name=\"6a2213371183f\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Hover<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you want your CoDrone EDU to hover for more time before landing, you can use the <strong>hover<\/strong> block from the flight commands menu and connect it after takeoff. <em>Don&#8217;t forget to type in the number of seconds you would like your CoDrone EDU to hover for before landing.<\/em><\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;8956&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22133711899\" name=\"6a22133711899\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Wait<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Using the <strong>hover<\/strong> block is one way to make your program pause for a duration of seconds. You can also use a<strong> wait<\/strong> block, found in the gray &#8220;Timing&#8221; category. This block will pause your program. No other commands will be sent until the delay finishes.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;8960&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]Replace the <strong>hover<\/strong> block with a <strong>wait<\/strong> block for 4 seconds. <em>What do you observe?<\/em>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;8961&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22133711910\" name=\"6a22133711910\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Emergency Stop<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1723611146177{padding-top: 20px !important;padding-right: 20px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;padding-left: 20px !important;background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-11766 alignleft\" src=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/icon_warning-150x150-2-84x85.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"106\" height=\"107\" \/><\/p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"><strong>WARNING<\/strong><\/p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\">Though this command should only be used in emergencies or when safety has become a concern, in this exercise, try to catch the drone when using the <strong>emergency stop<\/strong> block or clicking &#8220;Stop&#8221;. In all other circumstances, you should use the land command to bring your drone safely to the ground.<\/p>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">There might be times when your CoDrone EDU is about to crash into something, and you need to have it land before it does serious damage. If you want your CoDrone EDU to land before crashing, you can always use the stop button in your workspace. <\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12842&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]You can also use the <strong>emergency stop<\/strong> block, located under \u201cFlight Commands\u201d. However, we always recommend using the <strong>land<\/strong> block whenever possible if you want to protect your drone from damage.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213371198e\" name=\"6a2213371198e\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 9<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Challenge<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<b>Challenge: CoDrone EDU Push-ups<br \/>\n<\/b><\/p>\n<div>\n<div>Try to make your CoDrone EDU take off and land 3 times in a row with one code! Currently, your CoDrone EDU can do one push-up with the code you have.<\/div>\n<div><\/div>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<div><strong>Rules<\/strong><\/div>\n<div>1. The CoDrone EDU must completely leave the ground on takeoff.<\/div>\n<div>2. The CoDrone EDU must be completely back on the ground on landing.<\/div>\n<div>3. You must include a hover command between takeoff and landing.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221337119f0\" name=\"6a221337119f0\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 10<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Lesson Complete<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Congratulations! You&#8217;ve learned all about how to use the CoDrone EDU&#8217;s basic flight commands. Before moving on to the next lesson, let&#8217;s review some of the blocks that you learned about in this lesson:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Takeoff<\/li>\n<li>Land<\/li>\n<li>Hover<\/li>\n<li>Emergency Stop<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7547&#8243; img_size=&#8221;750&#215;670&#8243; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 11 We've Moved! [vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1761250576975{padding-top: 20px !important;padding-right: 20px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;padding-left: 20px !important;background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}\"] We\u2019ve moved to our new lesson portal: Robolink Learn! Lessons here&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/1-2-flight-events-junior-cde-blockly\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":4741,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":3877,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1817,1763,1777,1793,626,1533,1438,853,144,167,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2135,2108,4328,14401,14358,2112,2122],"class_list":["post-3935","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-beginner","lesson-tag-blockly","lesson-tag-cde","lesson-tag-cdej","lesson-tag-flight-commands","lesson-tag-flight-events","lesson-tag-programming","module-beginner","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3935","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":72,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3935\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":13612,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3935\/revisions\